[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: which stage are we losing the most deals at, by count and by value, and what does that tell us to fix?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-22 20:04:09\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.0s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [  1.0s]          found github__list_repositories\r\n  [  1.0s]          found posthog__list_events\r\n  [  1.0s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [  1.0s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n  [  5.3s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 13.2s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 13.2s] step 1   calling hubspot__closed_won\r\n  [ 13.2s] step 1   calling hubspot__pipeline\r\n  [ 13.2s] step 1   calling slack__search_messages query='lost deal'\r\n  [ 13.2s] step 1   calling slack__find_decision topic='deal stage losing'\r\n  [ 19.6s] step 1   got hubspot__search (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 19.6s] step 1   got hubspot__closed_won (5 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 19.6s] step 1   got hubspot__pipeline (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 19.6s] step 1   got slack__search_messages (7 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 19.6s] step 1   got slack__find_decision (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 19.6s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 23.3s] step 2   got read hubspot.search in full (100 rows) (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 23.3s] step 2   got read hubspot.pipeline in full (69 rows) (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 23.3s] step 3   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 69.2s]          drafting the report from 8 observation(s)\r\n  [122.9s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [122.9s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: skipped, this report asserts no cause (0.0s)\r\n  [131.4s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Which stage are we losing the most deals at, by count and by value, and what does that tell us to fix?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: low\r\nTook 123s over 3 steps, 80,477 tokens, 8 observations gathered, 3 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-------------------------------\r\n  By current pipeline concentration, 'presentationscheduled' is where the most deals and the most value sit unclosed \u2014 \u2588\u2588 deals worth $\u2588.\u2588M, more than double any other stage \u2014 but HubSpot does not record which stage a deal was in when it was actually marked closed-lost, so this is a proxy for stall risk rather than a direct measure of where deals are lost.  [hubspot.pipeline 977b17e4, hubspot.search 67613d01]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-------------------------------\r\n  HubSpot does not record the stage a deal was in when it was marked closed-lost  (medium)\r\n    - All \u2588\u2588\u2588 closed-lost deals in the search window carry stage='closedlost' uniformly, with no prior-stage field, so which pipeline stage actually produces the most losses cannot be measured directly from this data.  [hubspot.search 67613d01]\r\n    - Sales team commentary in Slack references ad hoc closed-lost tracking spreadsheets and re-engagement workflows built outside HubSpot's native stage field, consistent with this gap.  [slack.search_messages ad17dd16]\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-------------------------------\r\n  P\u2588 Add a 'last stage before closed-lost' property (or use HubSpot's deal stage history) so \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 loss analysis can identify the actual stage deals are lost from, rather than inferring it from where open deals currently stall.\r\n      why: Closed-lost records currently carry only a single terminal stage value, making it impossible to distinguish deals lost \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 in qualification from deals lost after a presentation or contract was sent.\r\n      [hubspot.search 67613d01]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-------------------------------\r\n  - The answer above is a proxy \u2014 the stage where the most open deal value currently sits \u2014 not a direct measurement of the stage where deals are actually marked closed-lost, because that field is not tracked. If deals stall at presentationscheduled but eventually convert, this would over\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 presentationscheduled as a 'loss' point.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- executive_summary[0]: The pipeline payload is truncated so we cannot confirm the exact count of \u2588\u2588 deals worth $\u2588.\u2588M in presentationscheduled or that it's more than double any other stage, though the cl\r\n- findings[1].claims[0]: The payload shows total_matching=\u2588\u2588\u2588 but only \u2588\u2588\u2588 records are returned (truncated), and all shown lack a prior-stage field, so the claim that all \u2588\u2588\u2588 uniformly lack this field is a\r\n- findings[1].claims[1]: The evidence shows one message referencing a personal 'cut' of \u2588\u2588 closed-lost deals with 'sales re-engage' tags, which supports ad hoc tracking outside HubSpot but does not mention\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-------------------------------\r\n  - Closed-lost deal search returned \u2588\u2588\u2588 total matching rows but only \u2588\u2588\u2588 were \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed in the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 call; the full \u2588\u2588\u2588 were not individually read, though the digest computed over all \u2588\u2588\u2588 rows shows uniform stage='closedlost' with no exceptions.\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-------------------------------\r\n  977b17e4  hubspot.pipeline  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?open=true\r\n  67613d01  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2026-03-22..2026-09-22&hs_is_closed_lost=true\r\n  ad17dd16  slack.search_messages  slack://search?query=lost deal\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (131s wall, 130s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey      